From: XCH27 <49464716+XCH27@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:02:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Catalog sources: the MCP Registry and Agent Skills
 repositories install as one-primitive plugins (OV-100 phase 2)

An mcp-registry marketplace source pages GET /v0.1/servers?version=latest
and turns each active server into a strict:false entry: npm, then PyPI,
then hosted HTTP/SSE, then OCI; required secrets become sensitive plugin
userConfig used only in env and headers, URL placeholders become
non-sensitive config, and a secret command argument skips that package.
Installing stages an empty root and writes the manifest from the entry,
so install, update and removal stay on the existing lifecycle. A folder or
repository without a marketplace manifest but with SKILL.md folders lists
each skill as a one-skill plugin; a folder that is itself a plugin is not
split. The Add marketplace dialog offers the official MCP Registry, and
catalog groups larger than 60 start collapsed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
